  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1136 AM MST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nAnother quick moving system remains progged to dig across the Great \nBasin Sunday night and continue across western Colorado through the \nday Monday and across eastern Colorado Monday night. This system \nlooks similar to today's system, as there is not a lot of available\nmoisture associated with it, and looks to bring another quick shot \nof light snow to mountains, with possible accumulations of 1 to 3 \ninches across the ContDvd, and another few inches possible across\nthe rest of the higher terrain, along with a few passing snow \nshowers across the plains. Temperatures remain cool behind this \nsystem on Tuesday, with dry conditions expected. \n\nModels continue to diverge for further into the Thanksgiving Holiday\nweek, with the GFS camp digging a system south across the Desert SW\nand into Old Mexico through Friday, with the EC and Canadian keeping\nanother weak trough translating across the Northern Rockies later \nWednesday, with moderate northwest flow aloft across the region on\nThanksgiving Day into next Friday. Latest NBM data seemingly splits \nmodel solutions keeping pops along the Continental Divide for \nThursday into Friday, with the plains dry. Highs look to warm back \ninto the 50s across the plains, with 30s and 40s across the higher \nterrain for Thursday and Friday. Time will tell.",
